{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -o '(.{0,140}(EX/MEM|EX.MEM|div_wait|wide|payload|bubble|mask).{0,160})' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"2:using variable\\narray indexing, followed by write-first bypass and x0 selection. These\\n32-bit read paths feed ID/EX every cycle and expose wide address-controlled\\nmultiplexers to FPGA synthesis. Shared address decoding and parallel data\\nselection offer a localized opportunity to improve timing withou\n2:using variable\\narray indexing, followed by write-first bypass and x0 selection. These\\n32-bit read paths feed ID/EX every cycle and expose wide address-controlled\\nmultiplexers to FPGA synthesis. Shared address decoding and parallel data\\nselection offer a localized opportunity to improve timing withou\n2:r each read port, decode its five-bit address once into mutually exclusive\\nselects for x1 through x31, shared across all 32 data bits. AND-mask each\\nstored word with its select and combine the terms with an explicitly\\nbalanced OR reduction tree rather than a serial accumulation or a priority\\nmux. Su\n2:ile.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the two indexed-array read muxes and serial read selection with\\nper-port shared one-hot address decoders, masked data terms, and an\\nexplicitly balanced OR tree. Make write-first bypass an exclusive\\nparallel term, omitting x0 from both stored-data and bypass selection.\n2:ile.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the two indexed-array read muxes and serial read selection with\\nper-port shared one-hot address decoders, masked data terms, and an\\nexplicitly balanced OR tree. Make write-first bypass an exclusive\\nparallel term, omitting x0 from both stored-data and bypass selection.\n3: completion\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"In cores/bench, hazard_unit freezes IF, ID, and EX whenever a memory\\ninstruction in EX/MEM encounters io_dmemReady=0. An aligned 