0: IF for hazard detection. Using the recovery-substituted ID instruction for these comparisons would indirectly put recovery into the slot's wide enable through `stall_if`; these outputs remove that path. ID still receives the prescribed NOP substitution.\\n- Kept the existing internal `stall`/`stall_if` \n30:names, now describing issue blocking. An empty fetch slot can fill while they are asserted.\\n- Inert payload can update on empty bypass or cancellation; validity alone determines whether it is retained work. Full occupied holds preserve the entire tuple.\\n- Gate sourc\n30: ten-iteration CoreMark: PASS for both implementations. CRCs: `e9f5/e714/1fd7/8e3a/fcaf`.\\n- Synthesized slot audit: 97 source bits; all 96 payload bits are plain DFFE registers sharing one enable. No reset, EX PC, or EX saved-prediction input reaches that enable's combinational leaf cone.\\n\\nThe extended \n30:s1_val[13]`; seed 3 terminates at ID/EX `ctrl.is_illegal`. This recovery-to-decode path is the measured timing concern; separating the slot payload enable did not remove the NOP-substitution data path required by the hypothesis.\\n\\n| Seed | Logic delay, ns | Routing delay, ns | Total, ns |\\n| --- | ---: | \n30:hrough recovery/NOP substitution into ID/EX became critical in all three seeds as median Fmax fell from 163.83 to 85.53 MHz; isolating slot payload enables does not remove recovery from the decode data path.\"}\n31:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260905-003-r10s2\", \"title\": \"Train the predictor from registered EX/MEM results\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Predictor history favors reducing update-path delay over adding accuracy:\\nthe return stack saved only 0.17% \n31:l three seeds to a 125.47 MHz median. Changing the\\nclassification boundary did not isolate the comparator from row fanout.\\n\\nThe existing EX/MEM bundle already registers the resolving instruction's\\nPC, architectural next PC, branch outcome, control-flow kind, and legality.\\nReusing these results can mo\n31:l three seeds to a 125.47 MHz median. Changing the\\nclassification boundary did not isolate the comparator from row fanout.\\n\\nThe existing EX/MEM bundle already registers the resolving instruction's\\nPC, architectural next PC, branch outcome, control-flow kind, and legality.\\nReusing these results can mo\n31:in is uncertain and\\nmust be established by the full routed fitness product.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Source predictor training from the existing EX/MEM register rather than\\nlive EX resolution. Introduce one registered training-valid token in\\ncore.sv: reset clears it; every other edge assigns it the current\\n\n31:-enable or hold this token on pipeline stalls.\\nThe existing resolve_valid remains the advancing-EX event, qualified by\\nin.valid, !stall, !div_wait, and !reset, and continues to qualify immediate\\narchitectural recovery. Keep these live resolution signals available to\\nthe pipeline checker independently of\n31: the delayed training interface.\\n\\nConnect if_stage's training inputs to that token and the corresponding\\nEX/MEM fields: PC from ex_mem_w.pc, target from ex_mem_w.pc_next, branch\\nand jump flags from ex_mem_w.ctrl, taken from ex_mem_w.branch_taken, and\\nlegal from !ex_mem\n31:_w.ctrl.is_illegal. Use the EX/MEM control bundle before\\nMEM-stage memory-alignment processing. The registered architectural next\\nPC is the exact target for legal jumps and taken branches, inc\n31:er write target storage. Preserve\\nEX's existing decoder and target-misalignment trap decisions.\\n\\nFor an instruction advancing at edge N, EX/MEM captures its results and\\nthe token becomes valid at N. The unchanged private row-event registers\\nand indexed target-event register accept this registered fee\n31: commit together at N+2. This adds exactly one\\ntraining-visibility cycle to the current N+1 commit. At N+1, capture must\\nsee the pre-edge EX/MEM payload even if a newer instruction advances on\\nthat same edge. Consecutive advancing instructions can generate consecutive\\nvalid tokens: sustain one trainin\n31:g transaction per clock without a queue,\\nbackpressure, table-state snapshots, or maintenance forwarding.\\n\\nUse the independent token, not EX/MEM.valid or MEM acceptance, to identify\\nnew training work. When EX/MEM holds for multiple data-bus stall cycles,\\nits older event is still accepted once and the \n31:eatedly. Likewise, an EX divide wait\\ncannot replay a token or suppress previously captured work. A younger\\nredirect, imem stall, load-use bubble, or backend hold must not cancel or\\npause older predictor events. Reset alone cancels the token and all\\nexisting pending/table validity, preventing pre-reset\n31:ral next PC.\\n\\nThe intended benefit is fewer live EX loads and a full register boundary\\nbefore predictor classification and fanout. Reuse EX/MEM payload registers\\ninstead of adding another wide raw-event bank; mapped state can still\\ngrow if previously unused EX/MEM fields become live. The unmeasured n\n31: frequency gain.\\nInspect synthesized and routed capture cones to confirm row-event and\\ntarget-event D/enables now originate in registered EX/MEM results and\\nthe token, without a live EX feedback bypass. Record all three timing\\npaths and LUT/FF counts; do not substitute source-level reasoning for\\na me\n31:: [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the independently refreshed training-valid register and wire the\\nIF training interface from EX/MEM.pc, pc_next, branch_taken, and ctrl\\nas specified. Retain live EX resolution and redirect signals for\\nrecovery and independent test observation. Do not qualif\n31:y delayed\\ntraining with current memory readiness, pipeline holds, or redirects.\\nReuse existing registered payload rather than duplicating it; keep\\nall external buses and the single-channel RVFI interface unchanged.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Update t\n31:efore its existing pending commit stage. Derive expected\\nevents from advancing EX and check their correspondence to the\\ndelayed token and EX/MEM payload, rather than trusting the new IF\\nwires as the oracle. Check target equality for target-writing events;\\nnon-writing events retain the oracle's stored \n31:: [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the independently refreshed training-valid register and wire the\\nIF training interface from EX/MEM.pc, pc_next, branch_taken, and ctrl\\nas specified. Retain live EX resolution and redirect signals for\\nrecovery and independent test observation. Do not qualif\n31:y delayed\\ntraining with current memory readiness, pipeline holds, or redirects.\\nReuse existing registered payload rather than duplicating it; keep\\nall external buses and the single-channel RVFI interface unchanged.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Update t\n31:efore its existing pending commit stage. Derive expected\\nevents from advancing EX and check their correspondence to the\\ndelayed token and EX/MEM payload, rather than trusting the new IF\\nwires as the oracle. Check target equality for target-writing events;\\nnon-writing events retain the oracle's stored \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
