{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20260905-001-r2s0','hyp-20260905-001-r7s0']:\n  print(d['id'])\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print(json.dumps(d['changes'],indent=2))\nprint('COREPKG',Path('cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv').read_text()[:2350])\nprint('ALU_TEST_START',Path('cores/bench/test/test_alu.py').read_text()[:6500])\nprint('PYTHON')\nimport importlib.util\nfor mod in ['yaml','jsonschema']:print(mod, bool(importlib.util.find_spec(mod)))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20260905-001-r2s0','hyp-20260905-001-r7s0']:\n  print(d['id'])\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print(json.dumps(d['changes'],indent=2))\nprint('COREPKG',Path('cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv').read_text()[:2350])\nprint('ALU_TEST_START',Path('cores/bench/test/test_alu.py').read_text()[:6500])\nprint('PYTHON')\nimport importlib.util\nfor mod in ['yaml','jsonschema']:print(mod, bool(importlib.util.find_spec(mod)))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20260905-001-r2s0\nMove the existing binary-to-operation decode across the ID/EX register.\nKeep the decoder's five-bit ALU operation encoding and legality rules,\nbut derive 19 individual selects in ID, one for each ALU_ADD through\nALU_REMU operation, and register them with the instruction in a dedicated\nid_ex_t field. Each select is a comparison against the existing encoded\noperation constant. For every accepted instruction the vector must agree\nwith dec_alu_op; it must hold during a data-memory stall and clear with\nthe existing reset/flush bubble. Do not derive instruction legality from\nthis vector or suppress the decoder's default ADD selection on traps.\n\nFeed those registered selects directly into the combinational ALU.\nReplace the binary-op case selection with parallel masked result terms\ncombined by a balanced OR reduction. Each term uses its corresponding\nselect bit directly; do not re-encode the vector, compare the complete\nvector with one-hot constants, or build a priority chain in EX. An\nall-zero vector returns zero. Preserve the existing arithmetic candidate\nexpressions, operand widths and signedness, shift masking, multiply-high\nvariants, divide-by-zero and signed-overflow handling. Keep all eight\nRISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS formulas and their operation mappings identical.\nThis is a control-decode retiming and selection rewrite, with no new ALU\npipeline stage, arithmetic algorithm, or instruction scheduling policy.\n\nPreserve operand forwarding, load-use bubbles, MEM/WB data retention\nduring stalls, branch resolution, predictor training and recovery, and\nthe architectural RVFI values. The sole intended gain is removing\nencoded-op decode from the measured EX timing path. Expect approximately\nsix percent higher fitness from higher Fmax, with unchanged CoreMark\ncycles for the same binary and ready schedule. This is an unmeasured\nestimate. Extra control flops, one-hot fanout, added ID decode delay, or\nan operand-to-result path becoming critical could erase the benefit.\n\nValidate the existing real-arithmetic ALU tests, decoder and pipeline\nsuites, unchanged ALTOPS formal gate, and stalled architectural cosim.\nCheck operation-select alignment through holds and flushes. Run the\nunchanged three-seed FPGA evaluation and compare median Fmax times the\nfull-precision iterations/bracketed-cycles ratio against 319.45; report\nLUT/FF changes and the new critical path. Keep benchmark configurations\ncomparable, and verify the specified 6 KB canonical CRCs, timing markers,\nand validation UART literal without changing evaluation files. Preserve\nnret=1, every external core port, and all hard invariants.\n\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n    \"description\": \"Add a 19-bit ALU operation-select field to id_ex_t only, with bits\\nindexed by the existing ALU operation constants. Retain the decoder\\nencoding and existing ctrl_t meanings; no select-vector state is\\nneeded in EX/MEM or MEM/WB.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\n    \"description\": \"Decode dec_alu_op into individual operation selects combinationally\\nin ID and capture them atomically with ID/EX. Reuse its existing\\nreset, flush, and hold priorities. Preserve the decoder and trap\\ncontrols, including default ADD on otherwise illegal instructions.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n    \"description\": \"Connect the registered operation-select vector directly to the ALU\\ninstead of supplying the encoded operation. Preserve both forwarded\\nsource values, ALU operand selection, result capture, PC+4 link\\nwrites, and all branch, stall, and predictor behavior.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\",\n    \"description\": \"Replace the internal ALU module's five-bit op input with the 19-bit\\noperation-select input. Select unchanged arithmetic candidates using\\nmutually exclusive masked terms and a balanced OR tree, returning\\nzero when all selects are clear. Preserve every real RV32IM result\\nand the exact corresponding ALTOPS formula. Add no state or latency.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\",\n    \"description\": \"Adapt the common drive helper to supply the one-hot bit for each\\nexisting operation index, mapping unsupported indices to all-zero\\nselection for default-result coverage. Retain every independent\\nexpected arithmetic result and corner-case assertion, including all\\nM-extension tests. Check zero selection and consecutive changes\\nbetween operation selects so stale or crossed selects are detected.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n    \"description\": \"Add directed instruction sequences with alternating ALU operations,\\nincluding MULH/MULHU/MULHSU and DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU, and verify exact\\nretirement results against independent expectations. Exercise these\\ntransitions through data-bus holds, instruction-bus stalls, load-use\\nbubbles, and misprediction flushes, checking that each advancing\\ninstruction retains its own operation select and that wrong-path\\noperations cannot retire or write memory. Preserve all existing\\nRVFI ordering, PC chaining, trap, and predictor assertions.\\n\"\n  }\n]\nhyp-20260905-001-r7s0\nMove the single predicate dec_alu_op == ALU_MULH ||\ndec_alu_op == ALU_MULHU || dec_alu_op == ALU_MULHSU across the ID/EX\nregister. Add a mul_high_sel bit to id_ex_t, preferably at its most\nsignificant end so existing lower field positions remain stable.\nCapture this predicate in ID with the control group: reset or flush\nclears it, a backend stall holds it, and ordinary capture updates it\nfrom dec_alu_op. Keep one sequential owner. Preserve the existing\nindependent wide-payload update rules and the five-bit ALU encoding.\nDo not use the auxiliary bit to determine instruction legality.\n\nWire the registered bit through EX into an additional internal ALU\ninput. Factor only the multiply-high contribution out of the main\nresult case. Keep all current integer, MUL-low, and DIV/REM case arms\nand default-zero behavior in a non_high_result path; omit the three\nhigh-product arms there, so that path is zero for their opcodes.\nSelect the high-product candidate using only op[1:0], whose current\nmapping is 00=MULH, 01=MULHU, 10=MULHSU, with 11 producing zero.\nCombine the two disjoint contributions as\n  out = non_high_result | ({32{mul_high_sel}} & high_result).\nThe registered class bit directly enables the high-result term;\ndo not reconstruct its five-bit opcode comparison in EX or qualify\nit with a second full-op decode. For every reachable instruction the\nregistered bit and opcode must agree, including bubbles and holds.\n\nPreserve the existing signed/unsigned product expressions, widths,\nand bit slices. In RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS, the same suboperation mapping\nmust select the existing MULH/MULHU add-XOR formulas and MULHSU\nsubtract-XOR formula with their exact constants. MUL-low and all\ndivider arithmetic, request/result handshakes, and the shared real\nand ALTOPS eight-edge schedule remain unchanged. This is one local\ncontrol-retiming optimization, with no new arithmetic algorithm,\ninstruction stage, execution latency, or predictor-policy change.\n\nExpect an unmeasured four-percent fitness gain through median Fmax\nalone. The intended mapped benefit is removing the measured encoded\nclass detector from the high-result selection path. Inspect synthesis\nand all three routed reports to verify that the registered select is\nactually used. Added ID decode delay, select routing, synthesis\nrefactoring, or the seed-2 recovery path becoming limiting can erase\nthe gain. Do not expand this into whole-ALU one-hot selection, opcode\nrenumbering, predictor changes, or synthesis keep constraints.\n\nRun the unchanged lint, real and ALTOPS unit suites, formal, stalled\ncosim, and three-seed FPGA gates. Check exact M-extension results and\nselect/op alignment through load-use bubbles, redirects, dmem holds,\nand divide waits. Require identical valid RVFI retirements with their\ncycle positions, accepted bus transactions, predictions, and bracketed\ncycles for matched ELF and ready schedules. Preserve nret=1, all\nexternal ports, decoder/trap rules, strict retirement order, memory\nbounds, markers, UART validation, and every protected evaluation file.\nCompute fitness with full-precision iterations/bracketed-cycles times\nmedian Fmax. Historical notes identify the recorded 388.66 comparison\nas a 2 KB score; keep that like-for-like comparison separate from the\nrequested unchanged 6 KB, -O3, ten-iteration run with both bus stalls,\nCRCs d4b0/be52/5e47, and the literal Correct operation validated.\n\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n    \"description\": \"Add one mul_high_sel field to id_ex_t only. Preserve all existing\\noperation constants, ctrl_t fields, and downstream bundle meanings.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\n    \"description\": \"Decode membership in MULH/MULHU/MULHSU before ID/EX and register\\nit with control reset/flush/hold priorities. Preserve the r5s0\\nseparation between control updates and wide-payload updates.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n    \"description\": \"Connect the registered multiply-high class bit to the internal\\nALU. Keep forwarded operands, link selection, divide interlocks,\\nfull EX/MEM bubbles, branch resolution, and training unchanged.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\",\n    \"description\": \"Accept mul_high_sel and extract only the three high-multiply\\nresult arms into a suboperation-selected contribution gated by\\nthis bit. OR it with the disjoint remaining result case. Retain\\nexact real products, ALTOPS formulas, and divider behavior.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\",\n    \"description\": \"Drive the new class input consistently at every opcode change,\\nincluding setup and divider input-perturbation tests. Retain all\\nexact real/ALTOPS vectors and handshake assertions. Add alternating\\nhigh-multiply, MUL-low, integer, and divide selections with signed\\nboundary operands to catch stale or incorrectly decoded classes.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"test/test_id_stage.py\",\n    \"description\": \"Extend reset/flush/stall priority checks to the new control bit,\\ncovering all three high-multiply operations and neighboring MUL\\nand DIV encodings. Assert alignment with the captured operation\\nindependently of payload capture, including flush plus hold.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n    \"description\": \"Update id_ex_t unpacking and assert the auxiliary selector agrees\\nwith the held or advancing opcode. Exercise high multiplies with\\nEX/MEM and MEM/WB forwarding, stalled-load dependencies, load-use\\nbubbles, redirects, divide waits, and reset. Preserve exact RVFI\\narithmetic, operands, PC chains, retirement order, bus effects,\\nand all existing prediction and cycle-level assertions.\\n\"\n  }\n]\nCOREPKG // rtl/core_pkg.sv\n//\n// Core-wide constants and pipeline-bundle types.\n//\n// Compilation-unit scope (no `package … endpackage` wrapper) because\n// Yosys's Verilog frontend rejects `import pkg::*;` even though it\n// accepts `pkg::sym` refs and package definitions. A file-scope\n// definition with an `\\`ifndef` guard is the lowest common denominator\n// across Verilator, Yosys, sby, and nextpnr-himbaechel.\n//\n// Order matters: this file MUST be the first source passed to any tool\n// (Verilator/cocotb runner / build.sh / formal staging). Subsequent\n// includes hit the guard and become no-ops.\n//\n// Latency:        n/a (declarations only).\n// RVFI fields:    none (defines types; no logic).\n`ifndef CORE_PKG_DEFINED\n`define CORE_PKG_DEFINED\n\n  // ── ALU operations ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_ADD    = 5'd0;\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_SUB    = 5'd1;\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_AND    = 5'd2;\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_OR     = 5'd3;\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_XOR    = 5'd4;\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_SLT    = 5'd5;\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_SLTU   = 5'd6;\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_SLL    = 5'd7;\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_SRL    = 5'd8;\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_SRA    = 5'd9;\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_LUI    = 5'd10;\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_MUL    = 5'd11;\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_MULH   = 5'd12;\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_MULHU  = 5'd13;\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_MULHSU = 5'd14;\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_DIV    = 5'd15;\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_DIVU   = 5'd16;\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_REM    = 5'd17;\n  localparam logic [4:0] ALU_REMU   = 5'd18;\n\n  // ── Branch operations (encoded = funct3 of BRANCH opcode) ───────────────\n  // Phase 1 only references BR_BEQ (decoder default). The rest are\n  // referenced by the EX-stage comparator in phase 2; we keep them here\n  // for documentation and silence UNUSEDPARAM until then.\n  localparam logic [2:0] BR_BEQ  = 3'd0;\n  /* verilator lint_off UNUSEDPARAM */\n  localparam logic [2:0] BR_BNE  = 3'd1;\n  localparam logic [2:0] BR_BLT  = 3'd4;\n  localparam logic [2:0] BR_BGE  = 3'd5;\n  localparam logic [2:0] BR_BLTU = 3'd6;\n  localparam logic [2:0] BR_BGEU = 3'd7;\n  /* verilator lint_on UNUSEDPARAM */\n\n  // ── Pipeline-bundle typedefs ────────────────────────────────────────────\n \nALU_TEST_START \"\"\"Unit tests for rtl/alu.sv.\n\nThe integer/multiply path is combinational. Divide/remainder uses the\nintegrated eight-edge engine, with the same handshake in ALTOPS builds.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport cocotb\nfrom cocotb.triggers import Timer\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport random\nimport tempfile\n\nimport pytest\nfrom cocotb_tools.runner import get_runner\n\nfrom _helpers import (\n    ALU_ADD, ALU_SUB, ALU_AND, ALU_OR, ALU_XOR,\n    ALU_SLT, ALU_SLTU, ALU_SLL, ALU_SRL, ALU_SRA,\n    ALU_LUI,\n    ALU_MUL, ALU_MULH, ALU_MULHU, ALU_MULHSU,\n    ALU_DIV, ALU_DIVU, ALU_REM, ALU_REMU,\n)\n\nMASK32 = 0xFFFFFFFF\nALTOPS = os.environ.get(\"ALU_ALTOPS\", \"0\") == \"1\"\nALT_MASKS = {\n    ALU_MUL: 0x5876063E, ALU_MULH: 0xF6583FB7,\n    ALU_MULHU: 0x949CE5E8, ALU_MULHSU: 0xECFBE137,\n    ALU_DIV: 0x7F8529EC, ALU_DIVU: 0x10E8FD70,\n    ALU_REM: 0x8DA68FA5, ALU_REMU: 0x3138D0E1,\n}\n\n\ndef _expected(op, a, b, real):\n    if ALTOPS and op in ALT_MASKS:\n        value = a + b if op in (ALU_MUL, ALU_MULH, ALU_MULHU) else a - b\n        return (value ^ ALT_MASKS[op]) & MASK32\n    return real & MASK32\n\n\nasync def _edge(dut):\n    await Timer(4, \"ns\")\n    dut.clock.value = 1\n    await Timer(5, \"ns\")\n    dut.clock.value = 0\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n\n\nasync def _setup(dut):\n    dut.clock.value = 0\n    dut.reset.value = 1\n    dut.div_req_valid.value = 0\n    dut.div_result_ready.value = 0\n    dut.op.value = ALU_ADD\n    dut.a.value = 0\n    dut.b.value = 0\n    await _edge(dut)\n    dut.reset.value = 0\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n    assert int(dut.div_req_ready.value) == 1\n    assert int(dut.div_result_valid.value) == 0\n\n\nasync def _check(dut, op, a, b, expected):\n    \"\"\"Drive op/a/b and check the combinational result.\"\"\"\n    dut.op.value = op\n    dut.a.value  = a & MASK32\n    dut.b.value  = b & MASK32\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n    actual = int(dut.out.value) & MASK32\n    expected = _expected(op, a & MASK32, b & MASK32, expected)\n    assert actual == expected, (\n        f\"op={op} a=0x{a & MASK32:08x} b=0x{b & MASK32:08x} \"\n        f\"expected=0x{expected & MASK32:08x} got=0x{actual:08x}\"\n    )\n\n\nasync def _check_div(dut, op, a, b, expected):\n    \"\"\"Count launch as edge one; perturb inputs and offer rejected requests.\"\"\"\n    expected = _expected(op, a & MASK32, b & MASK32, expected)\n    dut.op.value = op\n    dut.a.value = a & MASK32\n    dut.b.value = b & MASK32\n    dut.div_req_valid.value = 1\n    dut.div_result_ready.value = 0\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n    assert int(dut.div_req_ready.value) == 1\n    assert int(dut.div_result_valid.value) == 0\n    for edge in range(1, 9):\n        await _edge(dut)\n        assert int(dut.div_req_ready.value) == 0, \"occupied engine accepted a request\"\n        assert int(dut.div_result_valid.value) == (edge == 8), f\"completion on edge {edge}\"\n        if edge < 8:\n            assert int(dut.out.value) == 0, \"partial/stale quotient published\"\n        else:\n            assert int(dut.out.value) == expected, (\n                f\"op={op} a={a & MASK32:08x} b={b & MASK32:08x}: \"\n                f\"{int(dut.out.value):08x} != {expected:08x}\"\n            )\n        # The op, operands, and a continuously offered request may all change\n        # while occupied. They must not change the saved calculation.\n        dut.a.value = (a ^ (0x12345678 * edge)) & MASK32\n        dut.b.value = (b + 12345 * edge) & MASK32\n        dut.op.value = (ALU_DIV, ALU_DIVU, ALU_REM, ALU_REMU)[edge % 4]\n\n    for _ in range(3):\n        await _edge(dut)\n        assert int(dut.div_result_valid.value) == 1\n        assert int(dut.div_req_ready.value) == 0\n        assert int(dut.out.value) == expected, \"unaccepted result changed\"\n    dut.div_result_ready.value = 1\n    await _edge(dut)\n    dut.div_req_valid.value = 0\n    dut.div_result_ready.value = 0\n    assert int(dut.div_result_valid.value) == 0\n    assert int(dut.div_req_ready.value) == 1\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def add(dut):\n    await _setup(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_ADD, 5, 3, 8)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_ADD, 0xFFFFFFFF, 1, 0)  # wrap\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def sub(dut):\n    await _setup(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_SUB, 10, 3, 7)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_SUB, 0, 1, 0xFFFFFFFF)  # borrow\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def bitwise(dut):\n    await _setup(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_AND, 0xFF, 0x0F, 0x0F)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_OR,  0xF0, 0x0F, 0xFF)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_XOR, 0xFF, 0x0F, 0xF0)\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def slt_signed(dut):\n    await _setup(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_SLT, 0xFFFFFFFF, 0, 1)              # -1 < 0\n    await _check(dut, ALU_SLT, 1, 0, 0)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_SLT, 0x7FFFFFFF, 0x80000000, 0)     # MAX > MIN\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def sltu_unsigned(dut):\n    await _setup(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_SLTU, 0xFFFFFFFF, 0, 0)             # max > 0\n    await _check(dut, ALU_SLTU, 0, 1, 1)\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def sll(dut):\n    await _setup(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_SLL, 1, 4, 16)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_SLL, 1, 31, 0x80000000)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_SLL, 1, 0x20, 1)                    # shamt = b[4:0] = 0\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def srl(dut):\n    await _setup(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_SRL, 0x80000000, 1, 0x40000000)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_SRL, 0x80000000, 31, 1)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_SRL, 0xFFFFFFFF, 0x25, 0x07FFFFFF)   # shamt masked\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def sra(dut):\n    await _setup(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_SRA, 0x80000000, 1, 0xC0000000)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_SRA, 0x80000000, 31, 0xFFFFFFFF)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_SRA, 0x7FFFFFFF, 1, 0x3FFFFFFF)\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def lui(dut):\n    await _setup(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_LUI, 0, 0x12345000, 0x12345000)\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def mul(dut):\n    await _setup(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_MUL, 3, 4, 12)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_MUL, 0xFFFFFFFF, 0xFFFFFFFF, 1)      # (-1)*(-1) low\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def mulh(dut):\n    await _setup(dut)\n    # INT_MIN * 2 = -2^32; high half = -1\n    await _check(dut, ALU_MULH, 0x80000000, 2, 0xFFFFFFFF)\n    # INT_MIN * INT_MIN = 2^62; high half = 0x40000000\n    await _check(dut, ALU_MULH, 0x80000000, 0x80000000, 0x40000000)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_MULH, 1, 1, 0)\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def mulhu(dut):\n    await _setup(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_MULHU, 0xFFFFFFFF, 2, 1)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_MULHU, 0xFFFFFFFF, 0xFFFFFFFF, 0xFFFFFFFE)\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def mulhsu(dut):\n    await _setup(dut)\n    # signed -2^31 * unsigned (2^32-1) = -2^63 + 2^31 = 0x8000_0000_8000_0000\n    await _check(dut\nPYTHON\nyaml False\njsonschema False\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
