{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/v1/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n e=json.loads(line)\n if any(s in e.get('title','').lower() for s in ['div','cold','alu']):\n  print(json.dumps({k:e.get(k) for k in ('id','title','category','outcome','fitness','fmax_mhz','cycles','lut4','error')}))\n  if e.get('id')=='hyp-20260428-007-r4s0' or ('div' in e.get('title','').lower() and e.get('outcome')=='improvement'):\n   print('DETAILS:',e.get('hypothesis'))\n   print('NOTES:',e.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\": \"hyp-20260427-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Move DIV/REM off the single-cycle ALU path\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"fitness\": null, \"fmax_mhz\": null, \"cycles\": null, \"lut4\": null, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: selftest.elf\"}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260428-004-r4s0\", \"title\": \"Hot-Bit ALU Result Mux\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"fitness\": null, \"fmax_mhz\": null, \"cycles\": null, \"lut4\": null, \"error\": \"sandbox_violation: agent touched off-limits paths: ['test/_helpers.py']\"}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260428-010-r6s0\", \"title\": \"Cold Multi-Cycle DIV/REM Unit\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 375.43, \"fmax_mhz\": 159.92, \"cycles\": 4259618, \"lut4\": 5888, \"error\": null}\nDETAILS: {'motivation': 'The current best core still keeps DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU in the same\\ncombinational EX-stage ALU result path as ADD, address generation, branch\\ncompare support, and MUL. The generated FPGA critical paths are dominated by\\nlong EX-stage carry/mux structures, while the CoreMark timed loop is\\neffectively division-cold: the static binary has only a few DIVU sites, and\\nthose are in setup/printing paths rather than the hot matrix/list/state\\niteration body. Prior multiplier and MEM-lane rewrites showed that reshaping\\nalready-mapped hot datapaths can badly hurt placement; the better\\nmicro-optimization is to remove the cold divider/remainder hardware from the\\none-cycle ALU path entirely while leaving multiply and all RV32I operations\\nsingle-cycle.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Replace the real combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU cases with a small\\niterative divider/remainder unit that is only entered for those four ALU\\nopcodes. Normal RV32I operations, branches, jumps, loads/stores, and all MUL\\nvariants remain one-cycle and keep the current forwarding behavior. When a\\ndivide-class instruction reaches EX, freeze IF and ID, inject bubbles into\\nEX/MEM while the divider is busy so older instructions retire exactly once,\\nthen advance the original instruction metadata with the completed quotient or\\nremainder result. The unit must preserve RV32M divide-by-zero, signed\\noverflow, REM-by-zero, and signed remainder semantics. Under\\nRISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS, keep the same start/busy/done interlock visible to\\nformal while substituting the existing ALTOPS result formulas so the\\narithmetic proof remains tractable. The expected win is a higher median Fmax\\nfrom removing the FPGA divider from the universal EX path, with negligible\\nCoreMark cycle impact because timed-region division traffic is cold.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 6, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'Remove real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arithmetic from the normal combinational\\nALU result mux and leave ADD/SUB/logic/shift/compare/LUI plus all\\nmultiply variants single-cycle. Keep the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS formulas for\\ndivide/remainder results available to the new divider path, and do not\\nalter MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU bit semantics.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/div_unit.sv', 'description': 'Add a compact iterative RV32M divide/remainder block with start, busy,\\ndone, op, operands, and result signals. Handle unsigned and signed modes,\\nquotient versus remainder selection, divide-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1, and\\nREM overflow corner cases explicitly before or after the unsigned\\niteration as appropriate. Keep the implementation small enough that its\\nper-cycle subtract/compare path cannot replace the old divider as the\\nglobal EX critical path.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Detect divide-class ALU ops in EX, launch the divider once, and hold the\\ncurrent ID/EX payload stable until done. While busy, drive a valid=0\\nbubble into EX/MEM rather than holding the previous EX/MEM instruction,\\navoiding duplicate RVFI retirement and duplicate regfile writes. On the\\ndone cycle, latch the completed divide result into EX/MEM together with\\nthe original instruction metadata, pc_next, rs values, rd, and control\\nfields.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Add an EX long-operation interlock input from ex_stage. Stall IF and ID\\nwhile a divide/remainder is busy, release them on the divider done cycle,\\nand keep dmem-stall priority over starting or completing a divide so the\\nexisting memory hold behavior and forwarding assumptions remain intact.\\nDo not weaken redirect flushing, imem backpressure handling, or the\\nexisting load-use interlock.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Wire the divider busy/done interlock between ex_stage and hazard_unit\\nwithout changing the top-level core IO, RVFI NRET=2 port layout, strict\\nchannel-0 retirement ordering, or tied-off channel-1 convention.\\n'}]}\nNOTES: # Implementation Notes\n\n## What changed\n\n- Removed real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arithmetic from `rtl/alu.sv`; those ALU opcodes now produce a dummy zero in the one-cycle ALU path. ADD/SUB/logic/shift/compare/LUI and all MUL variants remain single-cycle, including the existing `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS` multiply substitutions.\n- Added `rtl/div_unit.sv`, an iterative RV32M divide/remainder unit with `start`, `busy`, `done`, opcode, operands, and result. The real hardware path uses one restoring subtract/compare step per cycle and explicitly handles divide-by-zero, signed INT_MIN/-1 overflow, REM-by-zero, and signed remainder sign correction.\n- Added the `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS` divide/remainder formulas to `div_unit.sv`. In ALTOPS mode the unit still exposes a start/busy/done interlock, but uses a short one-busy-cycle latency so the existing 20-cycle formal depths remain tractable.\n- Updated `rtl/ex_stage.sv` to detect divide-class ALU ops, latch the original ID/EX metadata plus post-forwarded source operands at launch, bubble EX/MEM while the divider is active, and inject the completed result with the original instruction metadata when done.\n- Updated `rtl/hazard_unit.sv` and `rtl/core.sv` to stall IF and ID while EX has a long operation pending. The existing dmem stall path still owns EX/MEM holding and MEM/WB valid suppression.\n- Updated cocotb tests so `test_alu.py` covers the one-cycle ALU and the old divide vectors moved to a new `test_div_unit.py`. `test_pipeline.py` now includes `div_unit.sv` in its source list and has a pipeline-level DIV/REM interlock and forwarding test.\n\n## Deviations\n\n- The formal ALTOPS divider intentionally does not run the full 32-cycle iteration. It keeps the launch/busy/done protocol visible while avoiding a liveness-depth failure in the default 20-cycle formal configuration.\n- I did not change the top-level `core` IO or RVFI NRET=2 channel layout.\n\n## Concerns\n\n- Real DIV/REM instructions now add roughly 33 cycles of latency for non-special cases. This matches the hypothesis assumption that division is cold in the timed CoreMark region.\n- The exact `bash formal/run_all.sh` invocation is blocked in this sandbox because `formal/riscv-formal` is a symlink to `/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/formal/riscv-formal`, which is outside the writable roots. The script failed before genchecks while trying to clear `formal/riscv-formal/cores/auto-arch-researcher/*.sv` with `Operation not permitted`.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `python3 -m pytest test/test_div_unit.py -q`: pass.\n- `python3 -m pytest test/test_alu.py -q`: pass.\n- `python3 -m pytest test/test_pipeline.py -q`: pass.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh`: blocked before formal solving by the read-only symlinked formal staging tree, as described above.\n- Equivalent formal run staged under `/tmp/codex-riscv-formal-6224` with the same generated file list and `formal/checks.cfg`: pass, 105 passed and 0 failed.\n\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260428-013-r7s0\", \"title\": \"Cold High-Half Multiply Unit\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 235.89, \"fmax_mhz\": 100.48, \"cycles\": 4259618, \"lut4\": 6725, \"error\": null}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260428-019-r9s0\", \"title\": \"Hot-Cold ALU Opcode Split\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"fitness\": null, \"fmax_mhz\": null, \"cycles\": null, \"lut4\": null, \"error\": \"sandbox_violation: agent touched off-limits paths: ['test/_helpers.py']\"}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260428-043-r17s0\", \"title\": \"RTL-Only Hot/Cold ALU Opcode Split\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 529.35, \"fmax_mhz\": 183.12, \"cycles\": 3459314, \"lut4\": 5930, \"error\": null}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260428-052-r20s0\", \"title\": \"Funct3-Aligned Hot ALU Encoding\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 334.55, \"fmax_mhz\": 115.73, \"cycles\": 3459314, \"lut4\": 5896, \"error\": null}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260428-059-r22s1\", \"title\": \"Replay-Assisted ALU Pair Dual Issue\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"fitness\": null, \"fmax_mhz\": null, \"cycles\": null, \"lut4\": null, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: selftest.elf\"}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260428-062-r23s1\", \"title\": \"MEM-Wait Simple-ALU Skid Slot\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 469.85, \"fmax_mhz\": 161.58, \"cycles\": 3438981, \"lut4\": 5908, \"error\": null}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
