{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git diff --check\ngit status --short\nsed -n '1,32p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260905-002-r5s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260905-002-r5s1\ntitle: \"Separate ID/EX validity from the wide recovery payload\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current ID/EX register clears its entire packed bundle on reset OR\n  flush. In addition, IF replaces the entire instruction with a NOP on\n  recovery, putting redirect into instruction decode, register addressing,\n  and load-hazard inputs. Thus a one-instruction squash controls hundreds\n  of payload bits even though only the instruction's validity must change.\n\n  The structural history identifies this as a recurring timing limit.\n  hyp-20260905-002-r3s1 removed indexed predictor maintenance from the\n  critical paths but exposed hazard/divide control into ID/EX resets.\n  The current winner, hyp-20260905-002-r4s1, reports 156.62 MHz median\n  Fmax and 371.55 fitness. Its median seed has a 6.39 ns path from\n  predicted_next_pc[0] through mismatch/hazard control to an ID/EX\n  operand register's RESET pin. The other two seeds remain limited by\n  local predictor comparisons. Earlier store buffering saved only 0.75%\n  of cycles, and the divider split saved area without timed-cycle gains.\n  Separating instruction validity from payload transport directly attacks\n  the measured recovery fanout while retaining the current schedule.\nhypothesis: |\n  Restructure the IF-to-ID/EX boundary around a separate registered valid\n  token. Keep the current pipeline depth, single issue, exact accepted\n  prediction metadata, and one-younger-slot recovery. This experiment\n  changes squash distribution, with no predictor-policy, arithmetic,\n  memory-latency, or instruction-scheduling redesign.\n\n  In IF, always present raw imem_data as out.instr. Keep out.valid low\n  on flush or redirect, and preserve the existing PC update priorities:\n  reset, immediate EX redirect, then accepted predicted advancement.\n  Recovery must still override instruction-bus backpressure. Preserve\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,re,subprocess\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260905-002-r5s1.yaml')\nr=subprocess.run(['/usr/bin/ruby','-r','yaml','-r','json','-e','puts JSON.generate(YAML.safe_load(File.read(ARGV[0])))',str(p)],capture_output=True,text=True,check=True)\ndata=json.loads(r.stdout)\nschema=json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text())\n# Evaluate every validation keyword used by this repository's schema.\ndef validate(value, rule, at='\"'$'\"'):\n    supported={'\"'$schema'\"','type','required','properties','pattern','enum','minLength','minItems','items','description'}\n    assert not set(rule)-supported, (at,'unsupported schema keywords',set(rule)-supported)\n    kind=rule.get('type')\n    types={'object':dict,'array':list,'string':str,'integer':int}\n    if kind:\n        assert type(value) is types[kind], (at,kind,type(value).__name__)\n    if 'enum' in rule: assert value in rule['enum'], (at,'enum')\n    if 'pattern' in rule: assert re.search(rule['pattern'],value), (at,'pattern')\n    if 'minLength' in rule: assert len(value)>=rule['minLength'], (at,'minLength')\n    if 'minItems' in rule: assert len(value)>=rule['minItems'], (at,'minItems')\n    for key in rule.get('required',[]): assert key in value, (at,'missing',key)\n    for key,child in rule.get('properties',{}).items():\n        if key in value: validate(value[key],child,at+'.'+key)\n    if 'items' in rule:\n        for index,child in enumerate(value): validate(child,rule['items'],at+'['+str(index)+']')\nvalidate(data,schema)\nassert data['id']=='hyp-20260905-002-r5s1'\nassert data['category']=='structural'\nassert -50<=data['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']<=50\nfor change in data['changes']:\n    path=Path(change['file'])\n    assert not path.is_absolute() and '..' not in path.parts\n    assert (Path('cores/bench')/path).is_file(), path\nprint('PASS: YAML parsed; every applicable repository-schema constraint checked.')\nprint('PASS: exact ID, structural category, integer impact range, and six bench-relative change paths.')\nprint(str(p))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
