{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"I’m choosing to move multiply-high execution into MEM, using operands already captured in EX/MEM. This removes high-product selection from the fast EX result path; low-half `MUL` keeps its current timing. The inspected CoreMark ELF places multiply-high instructions only in initialization and printing, though the implementation must verify their timed frequency.\n\n"}}
