 were reviewed. Full registered\\none-hot ALU selection in r2s0, a registered multiply-high class bit in\\nr7s0, and link-result folding in r9s0 all regressed. The proposed change\\nuses the existing five control bits and an aligned M-extension encoding;\\nthe reviewed history contains no such encoding experiment. The current\\nMUL family occupies 11 through 14 and DIV/REM straddles 15 through 18,\\nmaking family membership irregular. Aligning both four-operation groups\\ncan simplify their selection and the divide interlock without extra\\npredecode registers or changes to arithmetic latency.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The saved winner in .tmp/thermometer-r6s0/baseline/cores/bench/rtl\\nmatches the current bench RTL byte for byte. Its routed seeds 1 and 3\\nlaunch from ID/EX alu_op[4] and alu_op[2] and end at EX/MEM\\nalu_result[25], taking 6.10 and 5.93 ns. The saved incoming reports in\\n.tmp/load-use-r10s0 show encoded operation selection passing through\\nseven mapped combinational cells. Seed 2 instead limits recovery into\\nID/EX.valid at 6.44 ns. This motivates a local operation-encoding and\\nresult-selection experiment, with unchanged instruction timing.\\n\\nLESSONS.md and the micro_opt log entries were reviewed. Full registered\\none-hot ALU selection in r2s0, a registered multiply-high class bit in\\nr7s0, and link-result folding in r9s0 all regressed. The proposed change\\nuses the existing five control bits and an aligned M-extension encoding;\\nthe reviewed history contains no such encoding experiment. The current\\nMUL family occupies 11 through 14 and DIV/REM straddles 15 through 18,\\nmaking family membership irregular. Aligning both four-operation groups\\ncan simplify their selection and the divide interlock without extra\\npredecode registers or changes to arithmetic latency.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Recode only the eight internal M-extension operation constants in\\ncore_pkg.sv. Keep all integer operations ADD through LUI at 0 through\\n10, ALU_ADD=0 for cleared controls, and the five-bit ctrl.alu_op width.\\nUse this exact mapping, matching RV32M funct3 in the three low bits:\\n  MUL=16, MULH=17, MULHSU=18, MULHU=19,\\n  DIV=20, DIVU=21, REM=22, REMU=23.\\nThus op[4:2]==3'b100 selects multiplication and 3'b101 selects\\ndivision/remainder. Codes 11 through 15 and 24 through 31 are unused\\nand must return zero without launching the divider. The instruction\\ndecoder already assigns symbolic constants inside validated matches;\\nretain those matches, all other controls, and default illegality.\\n\\nFactor the combinational ALU result into three exclusive contributions.\\nCompute integer_result with a case on op[3:0], keeping the existing\\neleven integer expressions at codes 0 through 10 and default zero.\\nCompute multiply_result with a case on op[1:0]: 00 selects MUL low,\\n01 selects MULH, 10 selects MULHSU, and 11 selects MULHU. Preserve the\\nexisting mul_ss, mul_su, and mul_uu expressions, widths, signedness,\\nand slices. Combine the results with parallel masked terms:\\n  out = ({32{!op[4]}} & integer_result)\\n      | ({32{op[4:2] == 3'b100}} & multiply_result)\\n      | ({32{(op[4:2] == 3'b101) && div_result_valid}} & div_result).\\nThis replaces the irregular full-op result case with local suboperation\\nselection and shallow family qualification. Do not repeat five-bit\\nM-operation equality tests inside these family-qualified result paths.\\nKeep fully defined defaults; introduce no X values or synthesis-only\\nbehavior to simplify unsupported operation codes.\\n\\nUse the same exact three-bit DIV/REM class comparison in ex_stage.is_div\\nand div_unit.legal_op. Preserve EX's in.valid and !is_illegal qualifiers\\nand every request/result-ready/reset/stall condition. In the real\\ndivider, signed_op may be legal_op && !op[0], and rem_op may be\\nlegal_op && op[1]. Preserve req_ready behavior even when an invalid\\noperation is offered; only acceptance is legal-op qualified. Leave the\\nrestoring datapath, accepting edge plus seven processing edges, saved\\noperands, corner cases, retained-result handshake, and controller exact.\\nThis class simplification is part of the same encoding experiment.\\n\\nIn RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS, the multiply suboperation selection must return\\nthe original instruction-specific formulas: MUL add-XOR 5876063e,\\nMULH add-XOR f6583fb7, MULHSU subtract-XOR ecfbe137, and MULHU add-XOR\\n949ce5e8. Retain all four existing divider ALTOPS formulas under their\\nnewly encoded symbolic constants and the same eight-edge controller.\\nIn particular, MULHSU and MULHU must not be swapped when adopting\\nfunct3 order. Both arithmetic builds must implement identical control\\nclassification and timing.\\n\\nAdd no pipeline state, stage, interface, instruction latency, or new\\nbypass. Retain the separate EX jump-link override, all target arithmetic,\\npredictor policy and training edges, forwarding, raw RVFI operands,\\nload-use detection, complete bubble-control clearing, and MEM/WB\\nforwarding-data retention. Preserve nret=1, every top-level port,\\ndecoder/trap/order discipline, bus handshakes, and every hard invariant.\\n\\nExpect an unmeasured three-percent fitness improvement through Fmax,\\nwith identical bracketed cycles for identical ELF and ready schedules.\\nConfidence is low: synthesis may reconstruct a deep selection network,\\nmultiplier sharing may change, and recovery, JALR, or predictor paths\\nmay dominate after remapping. Inspect synthesized class predicates,\\nall three routed critical paths, LUT4/FF counts, and MULT36X36 usage.\\nVerify whether the winner's single shared multiplier is retained;\\na simpler source expression alone is not evidence of a timing gain.\\n\\nRun unchanged lint, decoder and pipeline tests, real and ALTOPS ALU\\nsuites, formal, stalled cosim, and three-seed FPGA evaluation. Test\\nevery new M code and every unused internal code, including while a\\ndivide result is retained. Compare valid RVFI fields and cycle positions,\\naccepted bus transactions, predictions, and marker-bracketed cycles\\nagainst the incoming winner under matched inputs. Numerical operation\\ncodes inside pipeline bundles intentionally differ; architectural\\noutputs and cycle positions must not.\\n\\nCompute fitness as full-precision iterations/bracketed-cycles times\\nmedian Fmax_Hz. Prior implementation notes associate the historical\\n388.66 score with a 2 KB image; report that identical-image comparison\\nseparately from the required canonical 6 KB, ten-iteration, -O3 run.\\nKeep evaluator and benchmark sources unchanged. Require both bus stalls,\\nbounded accesses, accepted start/stop markers, CRCs d4b0/be52/5e47,\\nand the literal Correct operation validated. for the canonical run.\\n\",\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"fitness_delta_pct\": 3,\n      \"confidence\": \"low\"\n    },\n    \"changes\": [\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Reassign only the eight M-extension constants to the exact 16..23\\nfunct3-ordered mapping. Document the integer, multiply, divide, and\\nunused code ranges. Preserve integer constants, control width, and\\nall pipeline bundle layouts and reset-zero meanings.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Implement integer and multiply suboperation cases plus the three\\nexclusive masked result terms specified above. Preserve all real\\narithmetic expressions and divider wiring. Apply the corresponding\\nsuboperation map to the exact ALTOPS formulas. Return zero for all\\nunused codes and for incomplete divide results.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Replace only the four-operation divide classification with the\\naligned op[4:2] class comparison, retaining valid/legal qualification\\nand all existing sequential, handshake, operand, result, link,\\nredirect, and predictor-resolution behavior.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/div_unit.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Use the aligned DIV/REM class for legal_op and class-qualified low\\nbits for signed/remainder selection. Preserve legal request\\nacceptance, invalid-request rejection, all controller transitions,\\narithmetic, special cases, ALTOPS constants, and result retention.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\",\n        \"description\": \"Replace imports of the eight stale M-operation constants from\\n_helpers with explicit local constants for the new specified\\nencoding; leave _helpers.py untouched. Preserve existing arithmetic\\noracles and assertions. Cover all 32 internal codes, all multiply\\nsignedness variants, both ALTOPS and real results, mixed operation\\ntransitions, invalid requests, and unrelated or unused opcodes\\nwhile the divider is busy or retaining a completed result. Keep\\nexact eight-edge latency and result-consumption checks.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"test/test_decoder.py\",\n        \"description\": \"Define the same explicit new M-operation expectations locally\\ninstead of importing their stale values from _helpers.py. Check\\nall eight RV32M funct3 values against their specified internal\\ncodes and full controls. Preserve every existing legal/reserved\\nencoding, default-illegal, and SYSTEM assertion; change no helper\\nor protected correctness checker.\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n        \"description\": \"Add mixed integer/MUL/MULH/MULHSU/MULHU/DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU streams\\nwith immediate consumers, both forwarding sources, load-use\\nbubbles, memory holds, redirects, divide waits, and reset. Check\\nexact arithmetic and raw RVFI operands, one retirement per\\ninstruction, unchanged divider release timing, and absence of\\nspurious divide requests on integer operations or bubbles.\\nRetain existing control clearing, predictor, handshake, trap,\\nsource reporting, and retirement-order assertions.\\n\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Reassign only the eight M-extension constants to the exact 16..23\\nfunct3-ordered mapping. Document the integer, multiply, divide, and\\nunused code ranges. Preserve integer constants, control width, and\\nall pipeline bundle layouts and reset-zero meanings.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement integer and multiply suboperation cases plus the three\\nexclusive masked result terms specified above. Preserve all real\\narithmetic expressions and divider wiring. Apply the corresponding\\nsuboperation map to the exact ALTOPS formulas. Return zero for all\\nunused codes and for incomplete divide results.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Replace only the four-operation divide classification with the\\naligned op[4:2] class comparison, retaining valid/legal qualification\\nand all existing sequential, handshake, operand, result, link,\\nredirect, and predictor-resolution behavior.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/div_unit.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Use the aligned DIV/REM class for legal_op and class-qualified low\\nbits for signed/remainder selection. Preserve legal request\\nacceptance, invalid-request rejection, all controller transitions,\\narithmetic, special cases, ALTOPS constants, and result retention.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Replace imports of the eight stale M-operation constants from\\n_helpers with explicit local constants for the new specified\\nencoding; leave _helpers.py untouched. Preserve existing arithmetic\\noracles and assertions. Cover all 32 internal codes, all multiply\\nsignedness variants, both ALTOPS and real results, mixed operation\\ntransitions, invalid requests, and unrelated or unused opcodes\\nwhile the divider is busy or retaining a completed result. Keep\\nexact eight-edge latency and result-consumption checks.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_decoder.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Define the same explicit new M-operation expectations locally\\ninstead of importing their stale values from _helpers.py. Check\\nall eight RV32M funct3 values against their specified internal\\ncodes and full controls. Preserve every existing legal/reserved\\nencoding, default-illegal, and SYSTEM assertion; change no helper\\nor protected correctness checker.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Add mixed integer/MUL/MULH/MULHSU/MULHU/DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU streams\\nwith immediate consumers, both forwarding sources, load-use\\nbubbles, memory holds, redirects, divide waits, and reset. Check\\nexact arithmetic and raw RVFI operands, one retirement per\\ninstruction, unchanged divider release timing, and absence of\\nspurious divide requests on integer operations or bubbles.\\nRetain existing control clearing, predictor, handshake, trap,\\nsource reporting, and retirement-order assertions.\\n\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 338.82,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 142.82,\n  \"cycles\": 4215262,\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n  \"error\": null\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
