{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,170p' test/cosim/run_cosim.py\nrg -n 'rs1|rs2|COMPARE|compare|diff|fields' test/cosim/run_cosim.py\nsed -n '1,100p' formal/riscv-formal/checks/rvfi_reg_check.sv\nsed -n '1060,1108p' cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\nsed -n '1,150p' cores/bench/test/test_id_stage.py\"","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Drives both reference and Verilator model, diffs RVFI output.\"\"\"\nimport json, subprocess, sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ndef run_verilator(sim_bin, elf, maxcycles=50_000_000, timeout=120):\n    result = subprocess.run([sim_bin, elf, str(maxcycles)],\n                            capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout)\n    trace = []\n    for line in result.stdout.splitlines():\n        if line.strip():\n            trace.append(json.loads(line))\n    # returncode: 0 = ebreak + in-bounds, 2 = maxcycles hit, 3 = ebreak + OOB access.\n    # Only rc==0 means clean completion; rc==3 signals the CPU generated an\n    # out-of-bounds memory address that used to silently wrap.\n    completed = result.returncode == 0 and bool(trace) and trace[-1].get('insn') == 0x00100073\n    stderr_msg = result.stderr[-2000:]\n    if result.returncode == 3:\n        stderr_msg = (stderr_msg + '\\n[oob_access detected during simulation]').strip()\n    return trace, completed, result.returncode, stderr_msg\n\ndef run_reference(elf, max_insns=10_000_000):\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).parent))\n    from reference import RV32IM\n    cpu = RV32IM(); cpu.load_elf(elf)\n    trace = []\n    for _ in range(max_insns):\n        r = cpu.step()\n        if r is None:\n            return trace, False, 'reference_invalid_or_unsupported_instruction'\n        trace.append(r)\n        if r['insn'] == 0x00100073:\n            return trace, True, None\n    return trace, False, 'reference_max_insns_without_ebreak'\n\ndef _mismatch(i, ref, field, expected, got):\n    return {'passed': False, 'divergence_at': i,\n            'insn': hex(ref['insn']), 'pc': hex(ref['pc']),\n            'field': field, 'expected': hex(expected), 'got': hex(got)}\n\ndef compare(ref_trace, sim_trace, ref_completed=True, sim_completed=True,\n            ref_reason=None, sim_returncode=0, sim_stderr=''):\n    for i, (ref, sim) in enumerate(zip(ref_trace, sim_trace)):\n        # Direct-equality RVFI fields. trap/halt/intr/mode/ixl are included\n        # so that any future divergence (e.g., CPU starts asserting trap or\n        # misreports privilege mode) surfaces immediately instead of hiding\n        # inside fields cosim used to ignore.\n        for rf, sf in [('order', 'order'), ('pc', 'pc_rdata'), ('npc', 'pc_wdata'), ('insn', 'insn'),\n                       ('rd', 'rd_addr'), ('rd_wdata', 'rd_wdata'),\n                       ('rs1', 'rs1_addr'), ('rs1_rdata', 'rs1_rdata'),\n                       ('rs2', 'rs2_addr'), ('rs2_rdata', 'rs2_rdata'),\n                       ('trap', 'trap'), ('halt', 'halt'), ('intr', 'intr'),\n                       ('mode', 'mode'), ('ixl', 'ixl')]:\n            if ref.get(rf, 0) != sim.get(sf, 0):\n                return _mismatch(i, ref, rf, ref.get(rf, 0), sim.get(sf, 0))\n        # RVFI ALIGNED_MEM convention: mem_addr is word-aligned; byte offset is\n        # encoded in the shifted byte-lane mask. Reference ISS reports raw byte\n        # address + unshifted width mask (1 byte / 3 half / 15 word). Normalize.\n        byte_off   = ref.get('mem_addr', 0) & 3\n        ref_addr   = ref.get('mem_addr', 0) & ~3\n        ref_rmask  = (ref.get('mem_rmask', 0) << byte_off) & 0xF\n        ref_wmask  = (ref.get('mem_wmask', 0) << byte_off) & 0xF\n        ref_wdata  = (ref.get('mem_wdata', 0) << (byte_off * 8)) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n        ref_rdata  = (ref.get('mem_rdata', 0) << (byte_off * 8)) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n        # Always require ref/sim mem_*mask to agree: that's the source of\n        # truth for whether a memory op happened at all.\n        if ref_rmask != sim.get('mem_rmask', 0):\n            return _mismatch(i, ref, 'mem_rmask', ref_rmask, sim.get('mem_rmask', 0))\n        if ref_wmask != sim.get('mem_wmask', 0):\n            return _mismatch(i, ref, 'mem_wmask', ref_wmask, sim.get('mem_wmask', 0))\n        # mem_addr only matters when at least one mask is non-zero. With\n        # both masks 0 (no mem op — common on traps), an addr discrepancy\n        # is meaningless garbage. The trap field itself is checked above.\n        if (ref_rmask | ref_wmask) and ref_addr != sim.get('mem_addr', 0):\n            return _mismatch(i, ref, 'mem_addr', ref_addr, sim.get('mem_addr', 0))\n        # Only compare rdata bytes that are actually read. The reference keeps\n        # sub-word values unshifted; RVFI ALIGNED_MEM reports the full memory word.\n        if ref_rmask:\n            mask_bits = sum(0xFF << (j * 8) for j in range(4) if (ref_rmask >> j) & 1)\n            if (ref_rdata & mask_bits) != (sim.get('mem_rdata', 0) & mask_bits):\n                return _mismatch(i, ref, 'mem_rdata',\n                                 ref_rdata & mask_bits, sim.get('mem_rdata', 0) & mask_bits)\n        # Only compare wdata bytes that are actually written.\n        if ref_wmask:\n            mask_bits = sum(0xFF << (j * 8) for j in range(4) if (ref_wmask >> j) & 1)\n            if (ref_wdata & mask_bits) != (sim.get('mem_wdata', 0) & mask_bits):\n                return _mismatch(i, ref, 'mem_wdata',\n                                 ref_wdata & mask_bits, sim.get('mem_wdata', 0) & mask_bits)\n    if not ref_completed:\n        return {'passed': False, 'divergence_at': len(ref_trace),\n                'field': 'reference_completion', 'reason': ref_reason or 'reference_incomplete'}\n    if not sim_completed:\n        return {'passed': False, 'divergence_at': len(sim_trace),\n                'field': 'sim_completion', 'returncode': sim_returncode,\n                'reason': sim_stderr or 'sim_did_not_retire_ebreak'}\n    if len(ref_trace) != len(sim_trace):\n        return {'passed': False, 'divergence_at': min(len(ref_trace),len(sim_trace)),\n                'field': 'retirement_count',\n                'expected': len(ref_trace), 'got': len(sim_trace)}\n    return {'passed': True, 'retired': len(ref_trace)}\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    sim_bin, elf = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]\n    try:\n        ref, ref_completed, ref_reason = run_reference(elf)\n        sim, sim_completed, sim_returncode, sim_stderr = run_verilator(sim_bin, elf)\n        result = compare(ref, sim, ref_completed, sim_completed,\n                         ref_reason, sim_returncode, sim_stderr)\n    except (json.JSONDecodeError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired, OSError) as e:\n        result = {'passed': False, 'field': 'harness_error', 'detail': str(e)}\n    print(json.dumps(result))\n    sys.exit(0 if result['passed'] else 1)\n2:\"\"\"Drives both reference and Verilator model, diffs RVFI output.\"\"\"\n41:def compare(ref_trace, sim_trace, ref_completed=True, sim_completed=True,\n44:        # Direct-equality RVFI fields. trap/halt/intr/mode/ixl are included\n47:        # inside fields cosim used to ignore.\n50:                       ('rs1', 'rs1_addr'), ('rs1_rdata', 'rs1_rdata'),\n51:                       ('rs2', 'rs2_addr'), ('rs2_rdata', 'rs2_rdata'),\n76:        # Only compare rdata bytes that are actually read. The reference keeps\n83:        # Only compare wdata bytes that are actually written.\n107:        result = compare(ref, sim, ref_completed, sim_completed,\n// Copyright (C) 2017  Claire Xenia Wolf <claire@yosyshq.com>\n//\n// Permission to use, copy, modify, and/or distribute this software for any\n// purpose with or without fee is hereby granted, provided that the above\n// copyright notice and this permission notice appear in all copies.\n//\n// THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\" AND THE AUTHOR DISCLAIMS ALL WARRANTIES\n// WITH REGARD TO THIS SOFTWARE INCLUDING ALL IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF\n// MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHOR BE LIABLE FOR\n// ANY SPECIAL, DIRECT, INDIRECT, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES OR ANY DAMAGES\n// WHATSOEVER RESULTING FROM LOSS OF USE, DATA OR PROFITS, WHETHER IN AN\n// ACTION OF CONTRACT, NEGLIGENCE OR OTHER TORTIOUS ACTION, ARISING OUT OF\n// OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE USE OR PERFORMANCE OF THIS SOFTWARE.\n\nmodule rvfi_reg_check (\n\tinput clock, reset, check,\n\t`RVFI_INPUTS\n);\n\t`rvformal_rand_const_reg [63:0] insn_order;\n\t`rvformal_rand_const_reg [4:0] register_index;\n\treg [`RISCV_FORMAL_XLEN-1:0] register_shadow = 0;\n\treg register_written = 0;\n\n\tinteger channel_idx;\n\talways @(posedge clock) begin\n\t\tif (reset) begin\n\t\t\tregister_shadow = 0;\n\t\t\tregister_written = 0;\n\t\tend else begin\n\t\t\tif (check) begin\n\t\t\t\tfor (channel_idx = 0; channel_idx < `RISCV_FORMAL_CHANNEL_IDX; channel_idx=channel_idx+1) begin\n\t\t\t\t\tif (rvfi_valid[channel_idx] && !rvfi_trap[channel_idx] && rvfi_order[64*channel_idx +: 64] < insn_order && register_index == rvfi_rd_addr[channel_idx*5 +: 5]) begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\tregister_shadow = rvfi_rd_wdata[channel_idx*`RISCV_FORMAL_XLEN +: `RISCV_FORMAL_XLEN];\n\t\t\t\t\t\tregister_written = 1;\n\t\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\t\tend\n\n\t\t\t\tassume(rvfi_valid[`RISCV_FORMAL_CHANNEL_IDX]);\n\t\t\t\tassume(insn_order == rvfi_order[64*`RISCV_FORMAL_CHANNEL_IDX +: 64]);\n\n\t\t\t\tif (register_written && register_index == rvfi_rs1_addr[`RISCV_FORMAL_CHANNEL_IDX*5 +: 5])\n\t\t\t\t\tassert(register_shadow == rvfi_rs1_rdata[`RISCV_FORMAL_CHANNEL_IDX*`RISCV_FORMAL_XLEN +: `RISCV_FORMAL_XLEN]);\n\t\t\t\tif (register_written && register_index == rvfi_rs2_addr[`RISCV_FORMAL_CHANNEL_IDX*5 +: 5])\n\t\t\t\t\tassert(register_shadow == rvfi_rs2_rdata[`RISCV_FORMAL_CHANNEL_IDX*`RISCV_FORMAL_XLEN +: `RISCV_FORMAL_XLEN]);\n\t\t\tend else begin\n\t\t\t\tfor (channel_idx = 0; channel_idx < `RISCV_FORMAL_NRET; channel_idx=channel_idx+1) begin\n\t\t\t\t\tif (rvfi_valid[channel_idx] && !rvfi_trap[channel_idx] && rvfi_order[64*channel_idx +: 64] < insn_order && register_index == rvfi_rd_addr[channel_idx*5 +: 5]) begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\tregister_shadow = rvfi_rd_wdata[channel_idx*`RISCV_FORMAL_XLEN +: `RISCV_FORMAL_XLEN];\n\t\t\t\t\t\tregister_written = 1;\n\t\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\tend\n\t\tend\n\tend\nendmodule\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def divider_immediate_result_consumers(dut):\n    \"\"\"Arithmetic/MUL, load/store addresses and data, branches, and JALR.\"\"\"\n    consumers = [\n        (ADD(4, 3, 3), 128),\n        (ADDI(4, 3, 5), 69),\n        (LW(4, 3, 0), 0xA5A55A5A),\n        (SW(3, 0, 0x180), None),\n        (SW(1, 3, 0), None),\n        (BEQ(3, 3, 12), None),\n        (BNE(3, 0, 12), None),\n        (JALR(4, 3, 0), 16),\n    ] + [(MOP(f, 4, 3, 2), 256 if f == 0 else 0) for f in range(4)]\n    for consumer, expected in consumers:\n        for delayed in (False, True):\n            trace = {}\n            consumer_pc = 16 if delayed else 12\n            # For a delayed JALR the architectural link changes as well.\n            rd_expected = consumer_pc + 4 if consumer == JALR(4, 3, 0) else expected\n            program = {0: ADDI(1, 0, 256), 4: ADDI(2, 0, 4), 8: DIVU(3, 1, 2),\n                       consumer_pc: consumer}\n            if delayed: program[12] = NOP()\n            if consumer & 0x7F == 0x63:\n                program[consumer_pc + 4] = SW(1, 0, 0x184)\n                program[consumer_pc + 12] = EBREAK()\n            elif consumer & 0x7F == 0x67:\n                program[consumer_pc + 4] = SW(1, 0, 0x184)\n                program[64] = EBREAK()\n            else:\n                program[consumer_pc + 4] = EBREAK()\n            rets, mem = await _run(dut, program, {64: 0xA5A55A5A}, trace=trace)\n            _assert_div_flow(rets, trace, bounded=True)\n            [r] = [r for r in rets if r[\"pc\"] == consumer_pc]\n            if rd_expected is not None: assert r[\"rd_wdata\"] == rd_expected\n            if (consumer >> 15) & 31 == 3: assert r[\"rs1_rdata\"] == 64\n            if (consumer >> 20) & 31 == 3: assert r[\"rs2_rdata\"] == 64\n            if consumer == SW(3, 0, 0x180): assert mem[0x180] == 64\n            if consumer == SW(1, 3, 0): assert mem[64] == 256\n            assert 0x184 not in mem\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def divider_after_redirect_meets_successor_window(dut):\n    for divide in (DIV, DIVU, REM, REMU):\n        trace = {}\n        rets, mem = await _run(dut, {\n            0: ADDI(1, 0, -101), 4: ADDI(2, 0, 7),\n            8: BEQ(0, 0, 12), 12: SW(1, 0, 0x180),\n\"\"\"ID/EX control priority and payload independence, including flush+hold.\"\"\"\nimport itertools\nimport random\n\nimport cocotb\nfrom cocotb.triggers import Timer\n\nfrom _helpers import run_cocotb\nfrom test_pipeline import ADDI, BEQ, DIV, ECALL, JAL, LUI, LW, REM, SW, _id_fields\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def control_and_payload_priorities(dut):\n    rng = random.Random(0x1DEB0BB1)\n    instructions = [ADDI(9, 3, -17), LW(9, 3, 20), SW(9, 3, 24),\n                    DIV(9, 3, 7), REM(9, 3, 7), BEQ(3, 7, -20),\n                    JAL(9, 124), LUI(9, 0xABCDE000), 0xABCDE497, ECALL()]\n    previous = None\n    # Start with reset, then exercise every reset/flush/stall combination\n    # against nonzero operands, immediates, register addresses and metadata.\n    controls = [(1, 0, 0)] + list(itertools.product((0, 1), repeat=3))\n    for instr in instructions:\n        for reset, flush, stall in controls + [(0, 0, 0)]:\n            pc, prediction, rs1, rs2 = [rng.getrandbits(32) for _ in range(4)]\n            valid = rng.randrange(2)\n            dut.clock.value = 0\n            dut.reset.value = reset\n            dut.flush.value = flush\n            dut.stall.value = stall\n            dut[\"in\"].value = (pc << 65) | (prediction << 33) | (instr << 1) | valid\n            dut.rs1_data.value = rs1\n            dut.rs2_data.value = rs2\n            await Timer(5, \"ns\")\n            decoded = int(dut.ctrl_decoded.value)\n            payload = dict(pc=pc, predicted_next_pc=prediction, rs1_val=rs1,\n                           rs2_val=rs2, imm=int(dut.imm.value), rd=(instr >> 7) & 31,\n                           rs1_addr=(instr >> 15) & 31, rs2_addr=(instr >> 20) & 31,\n                           instr=instr)\n            dut.clock.value = 1\n            await Timer(5, \"ns\")\n            actual = _id_fields(int(dut.out.value))\n            if reset:\n                assert all(value == 0 for value in actual.values())\n            else:\n                for field, value in payload.items():\n                    assert actual[field] == (previous[field] if stall else value), (\n                        f\"{field}: flush={flush} stall={stall} payload mismatch\"\n                    )\n                assert actual[\"ctrl\"] == (0 if flush else previous[\"ctrl\"] if stall else decoded)\n                assert actual[\"valid\"] == (0 if flush else previous[\"valid\"] if stall else valid)\n            previous = actual\n\n\ndef test_id_stage_runner():\n    run_cocotb(toplevel=\"id_stage\",\n               sources=[\"core_pkg.sv\", \"decoder.sv\", \"imm_gen.sv\", \"id_stage.sv\"],\n               test_module=\"test_id_stage\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n    x=json.loads(line)\n    if x['id']=='hyp-20260905-001-r10s0':\n        h=x['hypothesis']; h=h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h\n        print(x['title']); print(h)\n        print('NOTES\\\\n'+x['implementation_notes'])\n        print('ERROR',x['error'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n    x=json.loads(line)\n    if x['id']=='hyp-20260905-001-r10s0':\n        h=x['hypothesis']; h=h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h\n        print(x['title']); print(h)\n        print('NOTES\\\\n'+x['implementation_notes'])\n        print('ERROR',x['error'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Suppress load-use bubbles for non-source instruction fields\nQualify the two existing load-use equality tests with combinational\ninstruction-format source-use bits. Add a seven-bit if_id_opcode input\nto hazard_unit and connect it to if_id_w.instr[6:0] in core.sv, using\nthe same instruction view as the existing source-address inputs.\n\nCompute uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 with a shallow opcode-only case, in\nparallel with the destination/source comparisons. Default both to one\nso unrecognized opcodes retain the existing conservative interlock.\nOverride the following exact seven-bit opcodes:\n  LOAD 0x03, OP-IMM 0x13, JALR 0x67: uses_rs1=1, uses_rs2=0.\n  LUI 0x37, AUIPC 0x17, JAL 0x6f, MISC-MEM 0x0f: both zero.\nOP 0x33, STORE 0x23, and BRANCH 0x63 retain both sources, including\nall RV32M operations. SYSTEM and unknown opcodes retain both sources.\nReserved funct encodings still pass through the unchanged decoder and\ntrap exactly as before; this format classifier never declares legality.\n\nReplace only the load-use condition with:\n  id_ex_mem_read && (id_ex_rd != 0) &&\n  ((uses_rs1 && id_ex_rd == if_id_rs1) ||\n   (uses_rs2 && id_ex_rd == if_id_rs2)).\nKeep source qualification separate from the full decoder's legality\nand control-result cones. Introduce no state, extra acceptance stage,\nor changes to source addresses, forwarding, or RVFI operand routing.\nIn particular, do not zero register fields to suppress comparisons.\n\nPreserve every remaining hazard output equation and its priority.\nA real load dependency still inserts one bubble when the backend is\nfree; memory/divide waits retain their existing hold behavior. Stores\nmust interlock on either address-base or write-data dependencies,\nbranches on either operand, and JALR on its base even when rd=x0.\nA load to x0 never causes a dependency bubble. Retain r5s0's complete\nctrl/valid clearing and payload capture on bubbles, instruction-to-NOP\nflushing, redirect priority, EX/MEM divide bubbles, and MEM/WB data\nretention during memory holds. Preserve nret=1, all external ports,\nordered retirement, traps, real/ALTOPS arithmetic, and all invariants.\n\nPredict an unmeasured one-percent fitness improvement, primarily from\nfewer cycles. Confidence is low because the dynamic false-dependency\nfrequency has not been measured and added opcode qualification can\nlengthen the fetch-to-interlock path or perturb placement. During\nevaluation, count false matches in the incoming design separately from\ntrue dependencies. Count an immediately removable bubble only when\ninstruction memory is ready and there is no redirect or backend hold;\noverlapping stall reasons must not be claimed as independent savings.\nCompare actual bracketed cycles rather than extrapolating this count.\n\nRun unchanged lint, unit, formal, stalled cosim, and three-seed FPGA\ngates. Directed tests must prove both removal of false bubbles and\nretention of every true dependency. Architectural results, used RVFI\noperands, PC chaining, and accepted memory effects must remain correct;\nretirement cycle positions intentionally can change. Check prediction\nrecovery against the prediction actually accepted with each instruction.\nMeasure Fmax, LUT4/FF cost, and routed critical paths with matched tools,\nELFs, and ready schedules. Compute fitness using full-precision\niterations/bracketed-cycles times median Fmax_Hz.\n\nThe experiment history identifies 388.66 as the scored 2 KB result.\nKeep that like-for-like comparison separate from the required canonical\n6 KB measurement without editing any evaluator or benchmark source.\nValidate the ten-iteration, -O3, 6 KB run with both bus stalls, accepted\nstart/stop markers, bounded accesses, CRCs d4b0/be52/5e47, and the UART\nliteral Correct operation validated. Make no changes outside the\nbench RTL and its allowed cocotb tests during implementation.\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 8, in <module>\nKeyError: 'implementation_notes'\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
