{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrows=[json.loads(s) for s in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\nfor r in rows:\n    print(r['id'], r.get('outcome'), r.get('fmax_mhz'), r.get('title'))\nr=rows[-1]\nprint('\\\\nLATEST IMPLEMENTATION NOTES\\\\n'+r.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"baseline-bench-609cf36 improvement 127.03 Baseline retest for cores/bench\nhyp-20260905-001-r1s0 regression 127.71 Balance register-file reads with shared one-hot address decoding\nhyp-20260905-002-r1s1 regression 133.89 Single pending-store slot with direct zero-wait completion\nhyp-20260905-003-r1s2 improvement 134.68 Small tagged target predictor with two-bit branch hysteresis\nhyp-20260905-001-r2s0 regression 129.4 Register one-hot ALU operation selects before execute\nhyp-20260905-002-r2s1 improvement 135.03 Split execution into a fast ALU and an eight-cycle divider\nhyp-20260905-003-r2s2 regression 124.94 Two-way target prediction at unchanged 16-entry capacity\nhyp-20260905-001-r3s0 regression 85.77 Localize predictor training to remove indexed feedback muxes\nhyp-20260905-002-r3s1 regression 143.41 Pipeline resolution feedback with registered predictor-row reads\nhyp-20260905-003-r3s2 improvement 147.75 Row-local predictor metadata training to remove the indexed feedback path\nhyp-20260905-001-r4s0 regression 126.15 Balance predictor training tag comparisons at LUT reduction boundaries\nhyp-20260905-002-r4s1 improvement 156.62 Pipeline row-addressed resolution events before local predictor updates\nhyp-20260905-003-r4s2 regression 145.99 Bank-local registered training commands for the target predictor\nhyp-20260905-001-r5s0 improvement 163.83 Remove wide ID/EX payload registers from bubble-control fanout\nhyp-20260905-002-r5s1 regression 110.22 Separate ID/EX validity from the wide recovery payload\nhyp-20260905-003-r5s2 regression 150.13 Eight-entry return stack with direct return recognition\nhyp-20260905-001-r6s0 regression 149.39 Replace local saturating-counter arithmetic with thermometer state\nhyp-20260905-002-r6s1 regression 97.2 Separate predictor tag validation from ordered metadata commit\nhyp-20260905-003-r6s2 regression 143.37 Eight-bit partial tags for the target predictor\nhyp-20260905-001-r7s0 regression 147.73 Predecode the multiply-high result class before execute\nhyp-20260905-002-r7s1 regression 145.6 Move PC-relative address generation across the ID/EX boundary\nhyp-20260905-003-r7s2 regression 150.94 Eight-entry target predictor with shorter lookup and less training fanout\nhyp-20260905-001-r8s0 regression 145.58 Select forwarded JALR targets after parallel operand additions\nhyp-20260905-002-r8s1 regression 153.8 Retime operand dependency matching across the ID/EX boundary\nhyp-20260905-003-r8s2 regression 108.97 Train bimodal direction counters independently of target tags\nhyp-20260905-001-r9s0 regression 124.67 Fold jump link values into the ALU result selection\nhyp-20260905-002-r9s1 regression 134.17 Execute multiply-high in MEM outside the fast EX result path\nhyp-20260905-003-r9s2 regression 125.47 Capture raw predictor events before update classification\nhyp-20260905-001-r10s0 broken None Suppress load-use bubbles for non-source instruction fields\nhyp-20260905-002-r10s1 regression 85.53 Decouple fetch from decode with one fall-through instruction slot\nhyp-20260905-003-r10s2 regression 143.66 Train the predictor from registered EX/MEM results\nhyp-20260905-001-r11s0 regression 148.06 Remove divide-bubble reset fanout from EX/MEM payload registers\nhyp-20260905-002-r11s1 regression 148.61 Move the complete multiply family into one shared MEM execution lane\nhyp-20260905-003-r11s2 regression 56.61 Prevalidate sequential and direct-target predictions in decode\nhyp-20260906-001-r12s0 regression 142.82 Align M-extension operation codes for shallow ALU class selection\nhyp-20260906-002-r12s1 regression 153.99 Rebuild the integer register file as replicated distributed RAM\nhyp-20260906-003-r12s2 regression 138.33 XOR-folded PC indexing for the existing tagged target predictor\nhyp-20260906-001-r13s0 regression 145.99 Remove false load-use bubbles with exact late RVFI operand forwarding\nhyp-20260906-002-r13s1 regression 150.17 Register integer and multiply results separately before final selection\nhyp-20260906-003-r13s2 regression 146.65 Validate sequential predictions from unflushed IF state\nhyp-20260906-001-r14s0 regression 138.73 Factor multiply signedness and result selection into a shared ALU candidate\nhyp-20260906-002-r14s1 broken None Resolve control flow in MEM from registered forwarded operands\nhyp-20260906-003-r14s2 regression 163.35 Separate predictor fetch tags from row-local training tags\n\nLATEST IMPLEMENTATION NOTES\n# Separate predictor fetch tags from row-local training tags\n\nImplemented the proposed storage replication. Correctness and locality checks\npass, but this three-seed trial does **not** meet the fitness acceptance\ncriterion: median Fmax is 163.35 MHz versus 163.83 MHz incoming, with identical\nbenchmark cycles. Fitness decreases **0.292986632484904%**. The implementation\nis retained for the orchestrator's evaluation.\n\n## Changes and policy preservation\n\n- `cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv`: widened the existing sixteen-word target\n  array from 30 to 56 bits, storing `{PC[31:6], target[31:2]}`. A single\n  asynchronous indexed read supplies both fetch tag equality and the aligned\n  target. Removed `tag_view` and the indexed fetch read of scalar row tags.\n- Added a 26-bit shared `pending_target_tag_q`, captured with the existing\n  target and index under exactly the existing `target_write` qualification.\n  The single synchronous write publishes both pending fields on the private\n  metadata commit edge. No pending or live-resolution bypass was added.\n- Private maintenance RTL is byte-identical to the incoming generate block\n  after removing its `tag_view` assignment. Validity, counters, full-tag\n  matching, all four commands, saturation, invalidation, and event ordering\n  are unchanged. Not-taken and invalidating events never write the RAM.\n- Reset still cancels capture and commit, clears all validity, and leaves\n  payload storage unreset. Pending validity drains independently of fetch\n  stalls, backend holds, and redirects. The new pending tag has no reset.\n- Logical table/event storage is 1360/525 bits versus 944/499. Module ports,\n  nret=1 retirement, accepted prediction transport, EX recovery, arithmetic,\n  scheduling, decoder legality, forwarding, and bus handshakes are unchanged.\n\n## Tests and local formal status\n\nThe existing independent integer-counter IF reference, pipeline predictor\noracle, and every existing prediction/timing assertion remain unchanged.\n\n`test_if_stage.py` adds pre-edge and post-edge public-output checks for\ncontinuous same-row aliases differing in every full tag bit, targets differing\nin every stored bit, simultaneous capture/commit/fetch, target retention,\nmatching/nonmatching invalidations, stalls, redirects, idle drain, reset with\na pending write and a simultaneous offered write, and subsequent allocation.\n\n`test_pipeline.py` adds a bounded three-iteration sequence with colliding\nbranches, changing load-forwarded JALR targets, nine data-memory hold edges,\nsix instruction-stall edges, three divides, and younger recovery while an\nolder jump commits. It checks exact public predictions, cycle-positioned\nretirement, strict order/PC chaining, unique resolution, targets, links,\noperands/results, accepted memory accesses, and absence of wrong-path stores.\n\nAn additional allowed test file, `test_prediction_compare.py`, replays directed\ntests and optionally compares complete incoming/candidate traces. No trace\nfields are omitted or normalized beyond JSON tuple conversion.\n\nValidation results:\n\n- Requested `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv\n  +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: **PASS**, no warnings.\n- Full cocotb suite: **10 pytest cases passed for each design**, including\n  real and ALTOPS arithmetic, five IF tests, and 38 pipeline tests.\n- Exact directed comparison: **48 runs, 1,557 cycles, 734 retirements,\n  125 recoveries**. All captured pipeline bits, public predictions, cycle\n  positions, RVFI fields, and accepted memory transactions agree.\n- **Local formal: PASS, 53 passed / 0 failed**, using unchanged\n  `bash formal/run_all.sh`, automatic nret=1 selection, `wrapper_si.sv`,\n  `checks_si.cfg`, and ALTOPS mode. Passed on the first attempt; no\n  counterexamples or RTL fix attempts. Multiplier/divider RTL was unchanged.\n- Unchanged `tools.eval.cosim`: **PASS**, selftest plus the evaluator's 2 KB\n  CoreMark CRC run, for both designs.\n- Additional selftest runs with both bus stalls at seeds 1, 42, and\n  0x13579bdf: **115 retirements each**, passing the unchanged Python ISS\n  comparison with exact incoming/candidate cycle-positioned trace equality.\n- All six FPGA runs completed through the unchanged synthesis script,\n  single-retirement benchmark wrapper, `nextpnr_run.sh`, and FPGA evaluator.\n\n## Mapped locality and resource cost\n\nThe mapped store is **14 RAM16SDP4 cells**, versus eight incoming. All 56\n`fetch_word` bits connect directly to RAM outputs. All 56 write-data bits\nconnect directly to the shared pending target/tag registers; every cell uses\nthe same pending write index, write enable, clock, and fetch read address.\nThere is no scalar `tag_view` net and no second memory lookup port.\n\nAll **416 private scalar tag flops** remain. Forward traversal through mapped\ncombinational cells, stopping at state boundaries, shows that every private\ntag bit reaches only its own row's maintenance endpoints. For example, row 0\npreviously reached 68 nonlocal state ports; the candidate reaches zero. The\nsame zero-nonlocal-endpoint assertion passes for all sixteen rows.\n\n| Measurement | Incoming | Candidate |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| nextpnr LUT4 resource use | 6,618 | 6,371 |\n| nextpnr FF resource use | 3,198 | 3,260 |\n| Explicit mapped flop cells | 3,150 | 3,176 |\n| Predictor RAM16SDP4 cells | 8 | 14 |\n| Other mapped memory cells, DPX9B | 4 | 4 |\n\nLUT4 use falls 247 (3.7322%). Explicit flop cells increase by the requested\n26 pending bits. The nextpnr FF resource metric increases 62; in both designs\nthat metric exceeds explicit flop cells by six per RAM16SDP4 cell. No extra\nRTL pipeline registers, vendor primitives, keep attributes, or synthesis\nscript changes were introduced.\n\n## Like-for-like benchmarks and fitness\n\nEach workload uses one identical ELF for incoming and candidate, built with\nthe unchanged benchmark Makefile using `COREMARK_OPT=-O3`, `ITERATIONS=10`,\nand total data sizes 2000 or 6000. Both use the unchanged harness with\n`--bench --istall --dstall` and default ready-schedule seed 0xdeadbeef.\n\nFitness is calculated as `(10 / bracketed_cycles) * (median_Fmax_MHz * 1e6)`\nusing unrounded iterations/cycle. The evaluator's displayed `ipc_coremark`\nis rounded and is not used in these calculations.\n\n| Measurement | Incoming | Candidate |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Seed 1 Fmax, MHz | 163.83 | 166.81 |\n| Seed 2 Fmax, MHz | 155.33 | 161.24 |\n| Seed 3 Fmax, MHz | 168.55 | 163.35 |\n| Median Fmax, MHz | 163.83 | 163.35 |\n| Historical evaluator 2 KB bracketed cycles | 4,215,262 | 4,215,262 |\n| 2 KB recoveries inside markers | 80,662 | 80,662 |\n| 2 KB recoveries, whole run | 81,398 | 81,398 |\n| 2 KB iterations/cycle | 2.372331779139707e-6 | 2.372331779139707e-6 |\n| 2 KB fitness, iterations/s | 388.6591153764582 | 387.52039612247115 |\n| Requested 6 KB bracketed cycles | 30,822,790 | 30,822,790 |\n| 6 KB recoveries inside markers | 550,409 | 550,409 |\n| 6 KB recoveries, whole run | 552,348 | 552,348 |\n| 6 KB iterations/cycle | 3.2443526364745047e-7 | 3.2443526364745047e-7 |\n| 6 KB fitness, iterations/s | 53.15222924336181 | 52.99650031681103 |\n\nThe unchanged historical evaluator reproduces **388.66 -> 387.52** for its\n2 KB workload. The requested canonical 6 KB result is reported separately.\n\nThe 6 KB accepted start/stop markers are at cycles **53,747 / 30,876,537**.\nBoth designs reach EBREAK after **22,093,920 retirements**, with `oob:false`,\nten iterations, `seedcrc=8a02`, `crclist=d4b0`, `crcmatrix=be52`,\n`crcstate=5e47`, `crcfinal=5949`, and the literal **Correct operation validated.**\nBoth runs contain 6,753,957 instruction-not-ready cycles and\n6,756,660 data-not-ready cycles.\n\nThe 2 KB accepted start/stop markers are at cycles **15,229 / 4,230,491**.\nBoth designs reach EBREAK after **2,937,037 retirements**, with `oob:false`,\nten iterations, `seedcrc=e9f5`, `crclist=e714`, `crcmatrix=1fd7`,\n`crcstate=8e3a`, `crcfinal=fcaf`, and the same validation literal.\n\nA read-only observer compiled from stdin and linked to each existing\nVerilator model includes the unchanged C++ harness. It checks committed\nprediction before/after every edge, exact accepted prediction through EX,\nunique issue/resolution/retirement, RVFI order and PC chaining, and the\nrequested narrow memory/MMIO bounds. It counts recoveries and hashes complete\ncycle/prediction/bus observations, cycle-positioned RVFI, and accepted memory\ntransactions. All assertions pass and all counts/hashes match between designs:\n\n| Workload | Accepted reads / writes | Cycle hash | RVFI hash | Memory hash |\n|---|---:|---|---|---|\n| 2 KB | 547,101 / 141,669 | 9936ace0ad8fc67a | 513e265fa104f6c4 | 8936b48ec7b30cd2 |\n| 6 KB | 3,824,882 / 817,301 | 143e55bdcdf56947 | 18443039de3d9b80 | b027e24e05e7b5d8 |\n\nHashes use 64-bit FNV-1a and supplement the exact bounded trace comparison;\nthey are not a formal equivalence proof. The observer adds the narrow\n`[0x10000000, 0x10000200)` MMIO bound without modifying the harness's bounds\nchecks. Its initial link needed the same weak-symbol flags used by the\nunchanged Verilator build; this was a validation-environment fix only.\n\nThe existing UART compiler-flags string is hardcoded to `-O2 -march=rv32im`;\nthe actual retained build logs show `-O3`. `CoreMark Size` prints the\nper-algorithm allocation, 2000 for the requested total 6000 and 666 for total\n2000. These contract-side reporting strings were not edited.\n\n## Routed critical paths\n\nFinal post-route register-to-register paths:\n\n| Design / seed | Source -> destination | Delay ns | Logic / routing ns |\n|---|---|---:|---:|\n| Incoming 1 | ID/EX alu_op[4] -> EX/MEM alu_result[25].D | 6.10 | 2.87 / 3.24 |\n| Incoming 2 | ID/EX predicted_next_pc[3] -> ID/EX valid.RESET | 6.44 | 2.77 / 3.67 |\n| Incoming 3 | ID/EX alu_op[2] -> EX/MEM alu_result[25].D | 5.93 | 2.78 / 3.15 |\n| Candidate 1 | Predictor row 12 valid -> row 12 counter[0].CE | 5.99 | 2.39 / 3.61 |\n| Candidate 2 | ID/EX alu_op[3] -> EX/MEM alu_result[0].D | 6.20 | 3.77 / 2.43 |\n| Candidate 3 | ID/EX predicted_next_pc[18] -> ID/EX valid.RESET | 6.12 | 2.77 / 3.36 |\n\nCandidate endpoints are respectively\n`cpu.u_if.metadata[12].counter_q_DFFSE_Q_1.CE`,\n`cpu.u_ex.reg_q_DFFR_Q_95.D`, and\n`cpu.u_id.reg_q_DFFRE_Q_192.RESET`. Their sources are\n`cpu.u_if.metadata[12].valid_q_DFFRE_Q.Q`,\n`cpu.u_id.reg_q_DFFRE_Q_194.Q`, and `cpu.u_id.reg_q_DFFRE_Q_77.Q`.\nThe fetch tag mux is removed, but local maintenance, ALU selection, and\nprediction recovery still limit these placements. Lower LUT use therefore\ndoes not establish the proposed clock improvement.\n\n## Deviations, concerns, and retained evidence\n\nThere is no architectural deviation. The extra trace-comparison test is\nwithin the allowed test surface. Checks ran in isolated scratch copies under\n`$TMPDIR/fetch-tags-r14s2/` to avoid generated writes into shared formal,\nbenchmark, tool, or other-core directories. All measured candidate RTL/tests\nmatch the worktree. A byte comparison verified 479 copied contract/reference\nfiles against their originals.\n\nThe requested implementation notes are in the current worktree directory.\nAll source changes are confined to bench RTL and `test_*.py` files.\n\nRetained evidence includes `formal.log`, both test/cosim/FPGA evaluation logs,\nthe formal per-check PASS statuses, `incoming-directed.json`,\n`candidate-directed.json`, `stalled-selftest.json`, `mapped-locality.json`,\n`timing-summary.json`, `fitness-summary.json` with full-precision decimal\nfitness, all six `nextpnr.log`/mapped/routed JSON artifacts,\nboth benchmark build logs, and `{incoming,candidate}-{2,6}k-measurement.json`.\n\nThe measured 2 KB ELF SHA-256 is\n`dcdb665667da1c6a868857c96a9eda17af9dcd779a6445d457f34a074d7ebf59`.\nThe measured 6 KB ELF SHA-256 is\n`30ef880019ab96effb260b04eb234a610b3447e4e7d2973c0f331eb34b1b59e2`.\n\nThe intended locality is confirmed, with unchanged execution behavior on the\ntested schedules. Added RAM resources and changed mapping/placement did not\nproduce a higher median clock/cycle product in this trial. No policy changes\nor evaluation changes were made to improve the reported result.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
